# Routing System Guide

## Route Definition

Routes are defined in `routes.json` files within each module at [Body/{role}/{module}/routes.json](mdc:Body).

### Basic Route Structure
```json
{
  "routes": [
    {
      "method": "GET|POST|PUT|DELETE|PATCH",
      "path": "/path",
      "handler": "role/Module/Controller@method",
      "name": "route.name",
      "middleware": ["optional", "middleware"]
    }
  ]
}
```

### Handler Format
```
"handler": "{role}/{Module}/{Controller}@{method}"

Examples:
- "public/Home/Home@index"
- "admin/Dashboard/Dashboard@show"
- "api/User/User@create"
```

## Route Parameters

### Dynamic Parameters
```json
{
  "path": "/blog/{id}",
  "path": "/blog/{id:\\d+}",
  "path": "/user/{username:[a-z0-9_]+}",
  "path": "/post/{year:\\d{4}}/{month:\\d{2}}/{slug}"
}
```

### Accessing Parameters
```php
public function show(): void
{
    $id = $_GET['id'] ?? null;
    $username = $_GET['username'] ?? null;
    
    // Use the parameters
    $this->load->model('public/Blog/Blog');
    $post = $this->model_blog->getById((int)$id);
}
```

## Named Routes

### Definition
```json
{
  "path": "/blog/{id:\\d+}",
  "handler": "public/Blog/Blog@show",
  "name": "blog.show"
}
```

### URL Generation
```php
// In controllers
$url = Router::url('blog.show', ['id' => 123]);
// Returns: /blog/123

// In views
<a href="<?= Router::url('blog.show', ['id' => $post['id']]) ?>">Read More</a>

// With query parameters
$url = Router::url('blog.index', [], ['page' => 2, 'sort' => 'date']);
// Returns: /blog?page=2&sort=date
```

### Redirects
```php
// Redirect to named route
Router::redirectToRoute('blog.show', ['id' => 123]);

// Regular redirect
Router::redirect('/blog');
```

## Route Groups

### Group Definition
```php
Router::group(['prefix' => '/admin', 'middleware' => 'auth'], function() {
    Router::get('/dashboard', 'admin/Dashboard@index');
    Router::get('/users', 'admin/User@index');
});
```

### Nested Groups
```php
Router::group(['prefix' => '/api'], function() {
    Router::group(['prefix' => '/v1', 'middleware' => 'api'], function() {
        Router::get('/users', 'api/User@index');
        Router::post('/users', 'api/User@create');
    });
});
```

## Middleware

### Route-Specific Middleware
```json
{
  "path": "/admin/dashboard",
  "handler": "admin/Dashboard@index",
  "middleware": ["auth", "admin"]
}
```

### Global Middleware
```php
// In Index/index.php
Router::middleware(['csrf', 'session']);
```

### Middleware Class
```php
<?php

class AuthMiddleware
{
    public function handle(): bool
    {
        $registry = Registry::getInstance();
        $session = $registry->get('session');
        
        if (!$session->has('user_id')) {
            Router::redirectToRoute('login');
            return false;
        }
        
        return true;
    }
}
```

## Route Methods

### HTTP Method Shortcuts
```php
Router::get('/path', 'Controller@method');
Router::post('/path', 'Controller@method');
Router::put('/path', 'Controller@method');
Router::delete('/path', 'Controller@method');
Router::patch('/path', 'Controller@method');
```

### Any Method
```php
Router::any('/path', 'Controller@method');
```

### Multiple Methods
```php
Router::match(['GET', 'POST'], '/path', 'Controller@method');
```

## Route Caching

### Enable Caching
```php
// In Index/index.php
Router::enableCache();
Router::setCacheFile(ROOT . '/Storage/cache/routes.php');
```

### Automatic Caching
Caching is automatic in production (when `APP_ENV` != 'development').

### Clear Cache
```php
Router::clearCache();
// Or manually delete: Storage/cache/routes.php
```

### Save Cache
```php
// After loading routes
Router::saveCache();
```

## Route Information

### Get Current Route
```php
$currentRoute = Router::getCurrentRoute();
```

### Check Route Exists
```php
if (Router::hasRoute('blog.show')) {
    // Route exists
}
```

### Get All Named Routes
```php
$routes = Router::getNamedRoutes();
```

### Route Statistics
```php
$stats = Router::getStats();
// Returns: ['total' => 15, 'named' => 12, 'cached' => true]
```

## Common Patterns

### Resource Routes
```json
{
  "routes": [
    {"method": "GET", "path": "/posts", "handler": "Blog@index", "name": "posts.index"},
    {"method": "GET", "path": "/posts/create", "handler": "Blog@create", "name": "posts.create"},
    {"method": "POST", "path": "/posts", "handler": "Blog@store", "name": "posts.store"},
    {"method": "GET", "path": "/posts/{id}", "handler": "Blog@show", "name": "posts.show"},
    {"method": "GET", "path": "/posts/{id}/edit", "handler": "Blog@edit", "name": "posts.edit"},
    {"method": "PUT", "path": "/posts/{id}", "handler": "Blog@update", "name": "posts.update"},
    {"method": "DELETE", "path": "/posts/{id}", "handler": "Blog@destroy", "name": "posts.destroy"}
  ]
}
```

### API Routes
```json
{
  "routes": [
    {"method": "GET", "path": "/api/users", "handler": "api/User@index", "name": "api.users.index"},
    {"method": "GET", "path": "/api/users/{id}", "handler": "api/User@show", "name": "api.users.show"},
    {"method": "POST", "path": "/api/users", "handler": "api/User@store", "name": "api.users.store"},
    {"method": "PUT", "path": "/api/users/{id}", "handler": "api/User@update", "name": "api.users.update"},
    {"method": "DELETE", "path": "/api/users/{id}", "handler": "api/User@destroy", "name": "api.users.destroy"}
  ]
}
```

## Best Practices

1. **Always use named routes** for easier URL management
2. **Use route parameters with regex** for validation
3. **Group related routes** with common prefixes
4. **Apply middleware** for authentication and authorization
5. **Cache routes** in production for performance
6. **Use RESTful naming** for consistent API design
7. **Document complex routes** in comments
